| Test for !MLT: tries MLT on this machine, in a TaskWindow (the desktop
| keeps running: please try using it while the test runs). Double-click
| it. Everything it makes goes in <Wimp$ScrapDir>.MLTtest (about 30MB);
| delete it afterwards. Save the TaskWindow's text (Menu > Save) and send
| it back.
| Most useful with one of your own 1080p videos (at least 20 seconds), so
| first:  *Set MLTtest$Clip SDFS::Pi.$.Videos.clip/mp4
If "<MLT$Dir>"="" Then Set MLT$Dir <Obey$Dir>
Run <MLT$Dir>.!Boot
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 Error MLT needs SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later.
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0 Error MLT needs the ARMEABISupport module.
CDir <Wimp$ScrapDir>.MLTtest
Echo MLT engine test 2 (melt 7.42.0, riscos-reeledit test build 2)
melt -version
Echo (1080p on the VideoCore needs gpu_mem=128 or more in config.txt.)
Echo
Echo 1. Two 10 second 1080p clips, encoded on the VideoCore (h264_encvchiq)
Echo start <Sys$Time>
melt -profile atsc_1080p_25 colour:red out=249 -consumer avformat:/<Wimp$ScrapDir>/MLTtest/red.mp4 vcodec=h264_encvchiq vb=8M an=1
melt -profile atsc_1080p_25 colour:blue out=249 -consumer avformat:/<Wimp$ScrapDir>/MLTtest/blue.mp4 vcodec=h264_encvchiq vb=8M an=1
Echo end   <Sys$Time>
Echo
Echo 2. A 2 second crossfade between them, saved as a project (MLT XML)
melt -profile atsc_1080p_25 /<Wimp$ScrapDir>/MLTtest/red.mp4 /<Wimp$ScrapDir>/MLTtest/blue.mp4 -mix 50 -mixer luma -consumer xml:/<Wimp$ScrapDir>/MLTtest/project.mlt
Echo
Echo 3. The project's pictures, made as the editor's preview makes them:
Echo    VideoCore decoding (h264_vchiq)
mltbench /<Wimp$ScrapDir>/MLTtest/project.mlt
Echo    ARM decoding
Set MLT_AVFORMAT_PREFER none
mltbench /<Wimp$ScrapDir>/MLTtest/project.mlt
Unset MLT_AVFORMAT_PREFER
Echo
Echo 4. The project exported: VideoCore decoding and encoding
Echo start <Sys$Time>
melt /<Wimp$ScrapDir>/MLTtest/project.mlt -consumer avformat:/<Wimp$ScrapDir>/MLTtest/export.mp4 vcodec=h264_encvchiq vb=8M an=1
Echo end   <Sys$Time>
Echo    again, with at most one VideoCore decoder at a time (MLT_AVFORMAT_PREFER_MAX=1)
Set MLT_AVFORMAT_PREFER_MAX 1
Echo start <Sys$Time>
melt /<Wimp$ScrapDir>/MLTtest/project.mlt -consumer avformat:/<Wimp$ScrapDir>/MLTtest/export1.mp4 vcodec=h264_encvchiq vb=8M an=1
Echo end   <Sys$Time>
Unset MLT_AVFORMAT_PREFER_MAX
Echo    the exports: their sizes, then (if !FFmpeg's *ffprobe is set up) their frame counts (450 each)
FileInfo <Wimp$ScrapDir>.MLTtest.export/mp4
FileInfo <Wimp$ScrapDir>.MLTtest.export1/mp4
If "<Alias$ffprobe>"<>"" Then ffprobe -v error -count_frames -select_streams v:0 -show_entries stream=nb_read_frames -of csv=p=0 /<Wimp$ScrapDir>/MLTtest/export.mp4
If "<Alias$ffprobe>"<>"" Then ffprobe -v error -count_frames -select_streams v:0 -show_entries stream=nb_read_frames -of csv=p=0 /<Wimp$ScrapDir>/MLTtest/export1.mp4
Echo
If "<MLTtest$Clip>"="" Then Echo 5. (skipped: *Set MLTtest$Clip to one of your own videos to try it)
If "<MLTtest$Clip>"<>"" Then Obey <MLT$Dir>.ClipTest
Echo Done.
